# <<[ package_name ]>>-http

## Purpose

Owns only the public Axum and HTTP boundary for `<<[ repo_name ]>>`: routes, handlers, middleware, extractors, and HTTP DTOs.

## Key entrypoints

- `src/lib.rs`: mounts the public router, applies shared middleware, and exposes the public OpenAPI document.
- `src/public.rs`: owns public routes, HTTP DTOs, and OpenAPI operations.

## Edit here for X

- Add or change routes, handler functions, HTTP response codes, headers, request IDs, tracing middleware, and extractors here.
- Call app-crate use cases through `AppState` instead of placing business logic in handlers.
- Regenerate committed contracts and clients with the root `contract:generate` package script.

## Invariants

- Keep handlers thin and delegate domain work to `<<[ package_name ]>>`.
- Keep observability middleware at this HTTP boundary.
- Preserve `/health/live` for process liveness and `/health/ready` for dependency readiness.
- Never depend on `<<[ package_name ]>>-admin-http` or mount privileged routes here. Admin transport has a separate crate and binary deployment boundary.
- Return JSON errors through `<<[ package_name ]>>-http-common`; never disclose internal error chains.

## Common commands

- `cargo test -p <<[ package_name ]>>-http`
- `cargo test -p <<[ package_name ]>>-test-support --test http`
